 "timing_rationale": "Coincident: the surveys describe the year they are taken in and are published within months.",
 "tracker_interpretation": "The surveys disagree by their definitions more than by their findings; production rates near half (Menlo, IDC in 2026) sit beside abandonment rates of a third to a half (Gartner's forecast, S&P Global), and McKinsey's share of firms scaling AI is a different measure again.",
 "unit": "share",
 "unpublished_reason": "The surveys measure different things (production, abandonment, scaling), so no band can be written over them yet; the rows are on /series and in Ask, and the indicator publishes once two surveys with the same definition exist for two years.",
 "updated_at": "2026-09-25",
 "valve_measured": "product_to_adoption",
 "why_it_matters": "The step between a pilot and reorganised work is where diffusion stalls; the P&L measure beside it (MIT NANDA) asks a harder question, so the two are read together."
